==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|unlawful|-ly|id2=adverbial}} or {{af|en|un-|lawfully|id1=negative}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌnˈlɔːfəli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unlawfully.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a manner not conforming to the law.
#: {{ux|en|The deceased was '''unlawfully''' killed during a riot.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1877|author=R. Rae|title=Newport|section=40
|passage=Look here, my body-snatchers, you have '''unlawfully''' abridged the liberty of one of the sons of the sovereign State of New York!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1892|title=The Pacific Reporter|volume=27|page=538
|passage=The information charges that the said Flem Parker, on or about the 20th day of November, 1890, and before the filing of this information, at the county and state aforesaid, did willfully, '''unlawfully''', and feloniously enter a certain barn {{...}}}}

